# Git workflow

`CONTRIBUTING.md` wins if this rule disagrees with it.

## Branches and pull requests

- Target `main`.
- Use `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.
- Open the pull request as a draft. Leave it draft until CI is green for the surface you touched. Merge by squash.
- Name the issue. Use a closing keyword only when the pull request fully satisfies that issue.
- Do not put secrets in the pull request body.
- Do not invent inboxes, team handles, or GitHub users.
- If the change alters what actually runs on `main`, update `docs/architecture/implemented-vs-specified.md` in the same pull request.
- Review the full branch diff (`git diff <base>...HEAD`), not only the latest commit.
- Push a new branch with `-u`.

## Commit messages

```
<type>: <description>

<optional body>
```

Types: feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore, perf, ci.

## Safety

- Do not pass `--no-verify`.
- Do not force-push shared branches, including `main`.
- Keep the hard lines in `CONTRIBUTING.md`: fail closed; no secrets in logs; drafts never run; ADV-021; ADV-024; YAML is the only persisted workflow definition.

Run the tests for the surface you touched before asking for review. Commands are in `CONTRIBUTING.md`.
